# The trash tree PAX carries as /bin/trash, /bin/trash-list,
# /bin/trash-restore, /bin/trash-rm and /bin/trash-empty (tb03;
# tools/mktrash builds it).
#
# trash is a reversible rm in wolf (wolffe-lang/trash, the trash track):
# each item goes into the user's trash, ~/Trash, laid out as the
# FreeDesktop.org Trash specification lays one out, and trash-list,
# trash-restore, trash-rm and trash-empty look after it until it is
# emptied. It is held to trash-cli, run only as a program, on Linux, and
# to its own rows on PAX under KVM (its tests/pax/). Its clean room is the
# specification, POSIX and the manual pages (trash's README); PAX reads no
# more of its tree than building it needs.
#
# trash trunk c027df8 (2026-11-08): T0-T3, hardened against a power cut
# part-way and two commands at once (trash#4), and built reproducibly
# (trash#5): its static builds depend on the commit alone, whatever the
# checkout's path and whether an ld.lld is installed, and its own gate
# holds that by digest. Pinned in its own wolf-toolchain.toml at wolf
# 0.2.38 / lupin 0.1.60 / wolf-std d4a4d4ca (the std the wolf archive
# bundles). tools/mktrash builds it with THAT toolchain, through trash's
# own tools/build.py --static, in two checkouts, refusing two digests, and
# ships the stripped copies that build keeps. The digests below are the
# ones trash's own gate prints (its repro row, at c027df8), and
# tests/distribution holds the image to them:
#   trash f7c2cb3bae1a6188001cadcc96936e6d1ba5aa7e341cb6d27c3fd4f4bfc9d173 1853976
#   trash-list 589a0c19f0ea5b7447d64c380a74b20c1d67fb60596c51c4f9e9dae5b449ac94 1858072
#   trash-restore 6766edc011a2fe41ed15055032ebcd737a6b3f47aeb86d642a332d7be30a0d2f 1862168
#   trash-rm 5ec1aa88a948bfc1c10db3df5c18ecc10946c0399d08b6e1db990137af2299ff 1853976
#   trash-empty e0487877dbc103315383f0c1b447a1a26fb2c83232f4b0159ad3ea7619ace274 1866264
TRASH_REPO=https://github.com/wolffe-lang/trash
TRASH_REV=c027df8364befe0d0a4930427f8b8d3a8401e7d8

# Codeload source archive sha256 at TRASH_REV, read twice (tb03).
TRASH_SOURCE_SHA256=2bc57c82804478ba4752063c3a8dee6c1d898d756188ad16a173c2fbc4342e3c
